@page "/acceptable-use"
@layout MarketingLayout

<HeadContent>
    <SeoHeadContent Path="/acceptable-use"
                    Title="Acceptable Use Policy — Brainy"
                    Description="What Brainy must not be used for: illegal activity, abuse, unauthorized security testing, and other prohibited uses." />
</HeadContent>

<section class="mkt-hero">
    <div class="mkt-wrap">
        <span class="mkt-eyebrow mkt-rise">Trust</span>
        <h1 class="mkt-title mkt-rise mkt-d1" style="max-width: 16em; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.4rem);">
            Acceptable Use Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mkt-lead mkt-rise mkt-d2" style="margin-top: 1.1rem;">
            What Brainy is for, and what it must not be used for.
        </p>
        <div class="mkt-draft-notice mkt-rise mkt-d3" role="note">
            <span class="mkt-draft-notice__icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9888;&#65039;</span>
            <p>
                <strong>Draft &mdash; pending qualified legal review.</strong> This policy is product
                documentation describing intended acceptable use. It is not a finalized legal policy and has not
                yet been reviewed by qualified legal counsel for your jurisdiction.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mkt-section">
    <div class="mkt-wrap">
        <article class="mkt-changelog">

            <h2>Purpose</h2>
            <p>
                Brainy is a personal knowledge and productivity tool: a place to capture, organize, and act on
                your own notes, tasks, and projects. This policy exists so that everyone using Brainy, and the
                infrastructure and AI providers it depends on, can be used safely and lawfully.
            </p>

            <h2>Prohibited uses</h2>
            <p>You must not use Brainy to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Store, generate, or distribute content that is illegal in your jurisdiction.</li>
                <li>Harass, threaten, defame, or abuse another person, or store material intended to facilitate such abuse.</li>
                <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to another account, or to Brainy's infrastructure, source code, or the infrastructure of any subprocessor (including configured AI providers).</li>
                <li>Perform security testing, penetration testing, vulnerability scanning, or load testing against Brainy without prior written authorization from Brainy's operator.</li>
                <li>Upload malware, or content designed to disrupt, degrade, or interfere with Brainy or any other user's use of it.</li>
                <li>Use Brainy's AI features to generate content that impersonates a real person without their consent, or to create material intended to deceive or defraud.</li>
                <li>Circumvent or attempt to circumvent account, plan, or rate limits, or resell access to Brainy without authorization.</li>
                <li>Scrape or bulk-extract other users' content, or use Brainy in a way that violates the privacy of any third party.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>AI-specific expectations</h2>
            <p>
                AI features process only the content you explicitly submit through them (see
                <a href="/ai-transparency">AI &amp; Your Data</a>). Do not use those features to generate content
                that violates the prohibited uses above, and treat all AI-generated output as a draft that
                requires your review before you rely on or share it &mdash; AI can be wrong.
            </p>

            <h2>Reporting a concern</h2>
            <p>
                If you believe Brainy is being used in a way that violates this policy, or you have a security
                concern, report it through the deployment's designated support channel so it can be reviewed.
            </p>

            <h2>Enforcement</h2>
            <p>
                Violating this policy may result in a warning, suspension, or termination of your account, at the
                discretion of Brainy's operator, without prejudice to your right to export your data beforehand
                where reasonably possible.
            </p>

        </article>
    </div>
</section>
